(footprint "SW_Taiway_200_SPDT_CommonPin1"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "hand")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Taiway series 200 sub-miniature SPDT. Same land pattern as SW_Taiway_200_SPDT - three terminals in a line on 2.54, 10-48 UNS bushing (o4.80 thread) -> o4.95 panel hole - but numbered with PAD 1 ON THE CENTRE (common) terminal instead of pad 2. DEPRECATED: use SW_Taiway_200_SPDT for new designs. Kept because TM_LPG-MIX MK3 has four variation switches already routed to this numbering with a two-pin Switch:SW_SPST symbol, and the common sits on the centre terminal either way - which is all the switch itself cares about. Formerly called SW_100_SPDT, which was simply wrong: the Taiway 100 series is the Miniature range, .185 [4.70] terminal pitch and a 1/4-40UNS bushing, and would not fit this footprint or its panel hole.")
	(tags "toggle switch spdt spst on-on on-off-on subminiature taiway 200 eurorack deprecated")
